The C code implements a Smoothed Particle Hydrodynamics (SPH) algorithm with Barnes-Hut gravity optimization to simulate 
molecular cloud dynamics

1) Density Calculation using cubic spline kernel.
2) Pressure Calculation using Polytropic EOS.
3) Computes acceleration using Gravity and visocisty and pressure forces.
4) It uses LeapFrog Time Integration scheme.

INITIAL CONDITIONS:
{
  "simpara": {
    "output": "molecular_cloud_simulation.out",
    "num_frames": 500,
    "num_per_frames": 20,
    "particle": {
      "size": 0.01
    },
    "timestep": 1.0e-3,
    "constants": {
      /* Fluid properties */
      "rho": 1.0,         /* Reference density (normalized) */
      "k": 0.1,           /* Sound speed parameter - related to temperature */
      "mu": 0.01,         /* Dynamic viscosity - low for molecular clouds */
      "gamma": 1.0,       /* Equation of state exponent (1.0 = isothermal) */
      
      /* Gravitational properties */
      "G": 1.0,           /* Gravitational constant (in simulation units) */
      
      /* Domain properties */
      "domain_size": 10.0, /* Size of simulation domain in parsecs */
      
      /* Numerical parameters */
      "theta": 0.5,       /* Barnes-Hut opening angle (0.5-0.7 recommended) */
      "mesh_size": 50     /* Resolution of spatial mesh for neighbor finding */
    }
  }
}
